  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Systems Planning and Analysis has $341M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, recorded across 67 awards with an average award size of $5.1M. Obligations fell 7.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $318M of the total. Engineering Services is the largest market for the company, accounting for $230M in obligations, followed by All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $61.3M. Other markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $24M, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $22.6M, Building Inspection Services at $2.8M, and Software Publishers at $95.8K. Fiscal-year obligations have trended up from $132M in FY21 to a peak of $368M in FY25 before the FY26 to date total of $341M. Current-year totals are partial, and the figures presented are contract obligations except for award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did Systems Planning and Analysis perform year over year?",
        "body": "Systems Planning and Analysis obligated $341M in FY2026 to date, down 7.2% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $132M in FY21 to $368M in FY25, then moved to $341M in FY26 to date. The company received 67 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $5.1M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and what markets do they buy?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $318M. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $18.7M and the Department of Energy obligated $4M. Engineering Services is the largest market at $230M, followed by All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $61.3M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $24M."
      }
    ]
